"Design pinned (2026-08-09, user): (1) NO implicit accounts -- an unattached identity can do nothing until it explicitly creates an account (connect-and-play is gone); initial UI must offer login inputs AND a separate new-account input set. A dev escape hatch (inject accounts / other pre-made state per dev task) is story-only for now: dev-inject-premade-state. (2) Login confirmation protocol: only previous connections have any basis for trust; the new connection has none until they share theirs. Quorum: at least HALF of the previous connections (identities attached at request time -- snapshot the voter set) must accept; ANY explicit refusal fails the request immediately; final acceptance is DELAYED until all voters responded OR 30 seconds after the acceptance quorum was reached, whichever comes first. ALL of this state is modeled in the DB, and requests/responses are security records in persistent, never-pruned tables (regular tables, deliberately NOT flagged/treated as an ephemeral events table). Implementation notes: login_requests (pending/accepted/refused + quorum_reached_at/resolved_at), login_request_voters (snapshot), login_responses (one per voter, persistent), scheduled finalize reducer for the 30s delay; attach = insert into account_identities on acceptance."